          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਘੰਟਾ (ghaṇṭā) is Sanskrit ghaṇṭā, \"bell\", taken over whole, a tatsama; the hour is usually explained as named for the gong struck to mark it. The inherited Punjabi form is ghaṇḍā, \"a bell used to attract deer\" (CDIAL 4421)."
            }
          ]
        },
